      "writtenOn": "2026-02-06T01:17:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It would be nice if we could use RAII for this so we don\u0027t mess it up in future changes.\n\nA few ideas:\n\nLocal to function:\n\n```\nstruct cleanup {\n  ~cleanup() { \n    OPENSSL_cleanse(\u0026fp_enc_buffer, sizeof(fp_enc_buffer)); \n  }\n} cleanup_guard;\n```\n\nMore generic like [`absl::MakeCleanup`](https://github.com/abseil/abseil-cpp/blob/master/absl/cleanup/cleanup.h):\n\n```\ntemplate \u003ctypename F\u003e\nstruct ScopedCleanup {\n    F func;\n    ~ScopedCleanup() { func(); }\n};\n\nstatic enum ec_status fp_commit_template(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e context)\n{\n    ScopedCleanup cleanup([\u0026] {\n        OPENSSL_cleanse(\u0026fp_enc_buffer, sizeof(fp_enc_buffer));\n    });\n    // ...\n```\n\nLet\u0027s do it in a followup CL if you think it\u0027s worth it. There may be other places where this pattern could be useful.",
